title: FabianIntroLoop1-2
tags:
---

The man is still waving, even as you approach him. He stands next to a bench overlooking the void lake, Solster standing behind him.
-> "Hello?"
    Sasha: "Hello?"
    << if $PsychMajor == true >>
        The man seems relieved to be able to stop waving. He was afraid of making a bad first impression. Perhaps not an unfounded fear.
    << else >>
        The man seems relieved to be able to stop waving.
    << endif >>
    ???: Hello to you too! It's a pleasure to finally meet you Sasha. 
    Fabian: I'm Pastor Fabian Goldhirsch, and I'm here to pick you up from station
    << set $FabianMood += 1 >>
-> "Who are you?"
    Sasha: "Who are you?"
    << if $PsychMajor == true >>
        The man seems relieved to be able to stop waving. He's quick to answer your question. He's picking his words carefully. He really wants to make a good impression
    << else >>
        The man seems relieved to be able to stop waving. He's quick to answer your question.
    << endif >>
    ???: Oh right, I forgot, you must've never seen me before!
    Fabian: I'm Pastor Fabian Goldhirsch. I came here to pick you up from the station! Sasha, right?
    << set $FabianMood += 1 >>
-> "Stop waving. I can see you."
    Sasha: "Stop waving. I can see you."
    << if $PsychMajor == true >>
        The man is quick to obey. He seems stunned for a second, his cheery demeanour is a little soured, before he replies to you. 
        He's picking his words carefully. He really wants to make a good impression
    << else >>
        The man is quick to obey. He seems stunned for a second, his cheery demeanour is a little soured, before he replies to you.
    << endif >>
    ???: Right, I can see that you’ve seen me!
    Fabian: I'm Pastor Fabian Goldhirsch. I came here to pick you up from the station! Sasha, right?
-> Ignore him.
    Sasha: (Ignore him)
    << if $PsychMajor == true >>
        The man continues waving for just a little too long, before gradually stopping. Hesitantly, he speaks up for the first time
        You've rattled him. He's off-center now, physically and mentally. 
    << else >>
        The man continues waving for just a little too long, before gradually stopping. Hesitantly, he speaks up for the first time
    << endif >>
    ???: Uhm... Hi. You are Sasha, right? Sasha Yildiz?
    Fabian: I'm Pastor Fabian Goldhirsch. I came to pick you up from the station.
    << set $FabianMood -= 1 >>

<< if $FabianMood lte -1 >>
The man extends his hand in greeting, hesitantly as well.
<< elif $FabianMood gte 1>>
The man enthusiastically extends his hand in greeting. 
<< else >>
The man extends his hand in greeting. 
<< endif>>
<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
    Solster pastors and other religious authorities usually greet strangers with a hug, as a sign of welcome to the community.
    Is he unfamiliar with this tradition? Or does he think that you'd be more comfortable with this?
<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
    Seeing his cloak up-close, it is clearly a hand-me-down, not something he bought himself. 
    It's too big for him, and clearly unfitting for him aesthetically. Something pastel would more his style.
<< elseif $TechMajor == true >>
    His words and actions are pre-planned, as an automaton following its programming. //Is this too modern? Nah, they got computers at the science park
    He must have spent his time waiting for you preparing his whole introduction.
<< endif >>
-> Shake his hand.
<< if $FabianMood <= -1 >>
His hand trembles slightly. He adds his other hand to the handshake to keep it steady.
<< else >>
His handshake is enthusiastic too, but more restrained. A pastor's decorum.
<< endif >>
Fabian: I hope you had good travels! It must have been a long journey to get here.
Fabian: I know myself how slow the train can feel when you're excited to get to your destination.
<< if $FabianMood lte -1 >>
    He finishes off his sentence with a nervous chuckle.
<< elif $FabianMood gte 1>>
    He finishes off his sentence with a hearty chuckle
<< else >>
    He finishes off his sentence with a bright smile
<< endif >>
<< if $FabianMood <= -1 >>
-> Continue ignoring him.

<< else >>
-> Ignore him.

<< endif >>

-> “I’m still not entirely sure who you are, or why you’re here.”

-> ""
